---
layout: base.njk
title: Space Weather Info
pageClass: info
bgImagePath: /assets/img/bg-info.jpg
---

<section class="info-panel">
  <div class="info-panel__header">
    <div class="info-panel__kp-block">
      <span class="info-panel__kp-label">KP:</span>
      <span class="info-panel__kp-value kp-highlight kp-dynamic" id="info-kp">{{ spaceweather.kp }}</span>
    </div>
    <h2 class="info-panel__title">SPACE WEATHER CONDITIONS</h2>
  </div>

  <div class="info-panel__stats">
    <div class="info-stat">
      <span class="info-stat__label">SOLAR WIND</span>
      <span class="info-stat__value wind-dynamic" id="info-wind">{{ spaceweather.wind }} <span class="info-stat__unit">km/sec</span></span>
    </div>
    <div class="info-stat">
      <span class="info-stat__label">IMF Bt / Bz</span>
      <span class="info-stat__value">
        Bt <span class="bt-dynamic" id="info-bt">{{ spaceweather.bt }}</span> nT,
        Bz <span class="bz-dynamic" id="info-bz">{{ spaceweather.bz }}</span> <span class="info-stat__unit">nT</span>
      </span>
    </div>
    <div class="info-stat">
      <span class="info-stat__label">NOON 10.7cm RADIO FLUX</span>
      <span class="info-stat__value flux-dynamic" id="info-flux">{{ spaceweather.flux }} <span class="info-stat__unit">sfu</span></span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="info-panel__updated">
    Live data from <a href="https://www.spaceweather.gov/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">spaceweather.gov</a> &mdash;
    Build time: {{ spaceweather.lastUpdated }}
  </p>
</section>

<div class="charts-grid">
  <div class="chart-block">
    <h3 class="chart-block__heading">PLANETARY K INDEX — 72 HR HISTORY</h3>
    <div class="chart-block__img-wrap chart-canvas-wrap">
      <canvas id="kp-chart"></canvas>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="chart-block">
    <h3 class="chart-block__heading">SOLAR WIND SPEED &amp; IMF Bz — 24 HR</h3>
    <div class="chart-block__img-wrap chart-canvas-wrap">
      <canvas id="wind-chart"></canvas>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/chart.js@4/dist/chart.umd.min.js"></script>
<script src="{{ '/assets/js/charts.js' | url }}"></script>

<section class="info-explainer">
  <h2 class="section-heading">UNDERSTANDING THE DATA</h2>
  <dl class="explainer-list">
    <div class="explainer-item">
      <dt>KP INDEX</dt>
      <dd>A scale from 0–9 measuring global geomagnetic activity. KP ≥ 5 means a geomagnetic storm — aurora may be visible at lower latitudes. KP 9 is extreme.</dd>
    </div>
    <div class="explainer-item">
      <dt>SOLAR WIND SPEED</dt>
      <dd>Velocity of charged particles streaming from the Sun. Higher speeds (≥ 500 km/s) can compress Earth's magnetosphere and trigger aurora.</dd>
    </div>
    <div class="explainer-item">
      <dt>IMF Bz</dt>
      <dd>The north-south component of the Interplanetary Magnetic Field. Strongly negative Bz (southward) opens Earth's magnetosphere and fuels geomagnetic storms.</dd>
    </div>
    <div class="explainer-item">
      <dt>10.7cm RADIO FLUX</dt>
      <dd>A proxy for solar activity. Values above 150 sfu indicate high solar activity. Measured daily at local noon in Ottawa/Penticton.</dd>
    </div>
  </dl>
</section>
